# The release path. A pull request touching any of these needs review from the
# owner, because between them they decide what gets published and under whose
# authority — the environment gate in release.yml is only as strong as the
# review on the file that declares it.
#
# This is a review requirement, not a permission boundary. The boundary that
# actually holds is on npm's side: the trusted publisher is bound to the
# `npm-publish` environment, so a workflow edited to drop that environment
# cannot mint a token npm will accept. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
